{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2604.13015","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2604.13015","prefix":"10.48550","suffix":"arxiv.2604.13015","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2604.13015","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"arXiv","alternateIdentifier":"2604.13015"}],"creators":[{"name":"Niu, Yaru","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yaru","familyName":"Niu","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Fang, Zhenlong","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Zhenlong","familyName":"Fang","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Chen, Binghong","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Binghong","familyName":"Chen","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Zhou, Shuai","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Shuai","familyName":"Zhou","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Senthilkumaran, Revanth Krishna","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Revanth Krishna","familyName":"Senthilkumaran","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Zhang, Hao","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Hao","familyName":"Zhang","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Chen, Bingqing","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Bingqing","familyName":"Chen","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Qiu, Chen","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Chen","familyName":"Qiu","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Tseng, H. Eric","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"H. Eric","familyName":"Tseng","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Francis, Jonathan","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Jonathan","familyName":"Francis","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Zhao, Ding","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Ding","familyName":"Zhao","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Learning Versatile Humanoid Manipulation with Touch Dreaming"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"lang":"en","subject":"Robotics (cs.RO)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-04-14T17:54:17Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-04-15T01:10:23Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-04-27T15:02:49Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-04-28T01:52:04Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-08-17T06:33:01Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2026-08-18T01:17:33Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2026-04","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"Article","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"3","rightsList":[{"rights":"arXiv.org perpetual, non-exclusive license","rightsUri":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Humanoid robots promise general-purpose assistance, yet real-world humanoid loco-manipulation remains challenging because it requires whole-body stability, end-effector dexterity, and contact-aware interaction under frequent contact changes. In this work, we study dexterous, contact-rich humanoid loco-manipulation. We first develop an RL-based lower-body controller that serves as the stability backbone for whole-body execution during complex manipulation. Building on this controller, we develop a VR-based whole-body humanoid data collection system that integrates dexterous hands and tactile sensing for contact-rich manipulation. We then propose Humanoid Transformer with Touch Dreaming (HTD), a multimodal encoder-decoder Transformer that models touch as a core modality alongside multi-view vision and proprioception. HTD is trained in a single stage with behavioral cloning augmented by touch dreaming: in addition to predicting action chunks, the policy predicts future hand-joint forces and future tactile latents, with tactile-latent targets provided by an exponential moving average target encoder without requiring a separate tactile pretraining stage. This encourages the policy to learn contact-aware representations for dexterous manipulation. Across five real-world contact-rich tasks, HTD achieves a 90.9% relative improvement in average success rate over the stronger baseline for each task. Ablation results further show that latent-space tactile prediction is more effective than raw tactile prediction, yielding a 30% relative gain in success rate. These results demonstrate that our touch-dreaming-enhanced learning system enables versatile, high-dexterity humanoid manipulation in the real world. More information and open-source materials are available at humanoid-touch-dream.github.io.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.13015","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":2,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2026-04-15T02:17:15.000Z","registered":"2026-04-15T02:17:15.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-08-18T04:02:01.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"arxiv","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2604.13015","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[]}}}}